      ],
      "speech": "Then video models showed up, and the gap got worse. Say I want this orange cat to yawn. I can type “the cat yawns,” but text can't say when, how wide, or which way. The model makes that up. But a video model doesn't start from text. It starts from this: random static, one block per frame. That noise already decides a lot. Same prompt, different noise, different video. So what if the noise itself moved?"
    },
